    "_about": "THE RAM (2026-11-05, 2nd pass: the horns built here, one continuous ridged amber spiral round each ear; heavier legs, a deeper chest, a broader poll, the wool kept off the horn roots): the sheep's body plan, bigger -- the fleece heaped in lumps over barrel, chest, rump, neck and the tops of the legs; a Roman nose (the face bowed out along the bridge) under the wool cap, the ears straight out to the sides; thin legs to two toes; the curled horns and the tail kept SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- horn (1 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): sideways LEAVES (sharp.js `fin`), drooping a little, the hollow forward and down; the stalk ball gone, the roots faired.",
